In a remanufacturing context, Design for Maintenance ensures that products can be effectively serviced, inspected, and kept in optimal condition throughout their use phase, thereby maximising the quality and value of cores returned for remanufacturing. Products that are well-maintained during use arrive at the remanufacturing facility in better condition, reducing the extent of reconditioning required and improving the economic viability of the remanufacturing process. Poor maintenance during use can render a product unsuitable for remanufacturing altogether, diverting it to lower-value recovery pathways.